## Fixed — commit `a077dd09`

**The bug @ptt-proof found:** `push_to_talk(app)` built `$mic`/`$hidden` with plain `div.c(...)` before `View.set_captor()` runs in `App.render()` — so they silently appended to nothing (`View.js`'s own append guard, no throw, no console error).

**The fix:** gave both the exact same deferred, explicit append `devshell.js` already uses right next to this call:
```js
app.styles_loaded().then(() => {
	$mic.append_to(View.body());
	$hidden.append_to(View.body());
});
```

**Re-verification — partial, and I'm flagging the gap honestly:** `node --check` is clean, and the fix is a byte-for-byte structural match to `devshell.js`'s own already-proven-live append pattern. I could **not** re-run a live-DOM check myself: Servex currently has no running project for this worktree (`list_servers` shows no `push-to-talk` entry — it must have stopped after `ptt-proof` finished its run), `monorepo.localhost` serves `michael/dev` which hasn't merged this branch, and `node server.js` is blocked for agents by the server-guard hook. I logged this gap in `task.jsonl` and named the right next step: re-run `@ptt-proof`'s own `proof.mjs` against the worktree server once it's up again, to confirm `.ux-dictate-ptt-mic`/`.ux-dictate-ptt-hidden` now exist in the DOM.

Logged to `task.jsonl`, ending my turn.
